    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0207" n="157" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg157"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.48/680</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-17T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>312. Your 474, October 13, 7 p.m. As you have already been advised, United
                    States, Great Britain, and France are sharing joint expense of rationing
                    Murmansk and Archangel districts for the winter. The shipments you mention,
                    although the purchase was undertaken by the British, apparently represent
                    supplies for payment of which Government of United States will assume one third
                    responsibility.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
